          {
            "section": {
              "header": "ECS Game Programming",
              "content": [
                "Why use ECS for games? ECS stands for: Entities, Components, Systems. ECS is actually a software design paradigm. It can be used for all software, not just games. ECS uses composition-based design.",
                {
                  "section": {
                    "header": "Entity",
                    "content": [
                      "An entity is any object in the game - the Player, a Platform, a Tile, a Bullet, the Enemy.",
                      {
                        "section": {
                          "header": "Object Oriented Programming",
                          "content": [
                            "Object Oriented Programming (OOP) uses the concepts of Objects and Inheritance to implement specific functionality.",
                            "Object Oriented Design (in games) is the process of strictly using OOP in order to design the architecture of the game engine and the entities within it.",
                            "OOP / OO Design helps to manage data and code."
                          ]
                        }
                      },
                      "An Entity will be any object in the game. Each Entity will have an (x, y) position. Entity will be used as the base class for others, such as Tile or Player.",
                      "Entities could be Static or Dynamic. A Static Entity, such as a Rock or a Tree would stay still and not have a velocity. An example of a Dynamic Entity would be a Bullet, or the Player. They would have a velocity and a position that would be constantly changing."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "section": {
                    "header": "Component",
                    "content": [
                      "Components are properties that can be attached to Entities. ",
                      "Examples of Components are:",
                      [
                        "Position",
                        "Speed",
                        "Bounding Box",
                        "Health",
                        "Weapon",
                        "Damage"
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "Entity: an Entity is any object in the game",
                ["Player", "Platform", "Tile", "Bullet", "Enemy"],
                "Component: a Component is property attached to an Entity",
                ["Position", "Texture", "Animation", "Health", "Gravity", "Components are [b]PURE DATA[/b]"],
                "System: Systems are the code or logic that drives behaviour",
                ["Movement", "Rendering", "Sound", "Physics"],
                {
                  "section": {
                    "header": "ECS Example of Entity / Component",
                    "content": [
                      {"table": [
                        [{"th": "Entity"}, {"td": "   "}, {"th": "Components"}],
                        [{"td": "Player"}, {"td": "   "}, {"td": ["Position, Speed, BBox, Sprite, Health, Gravity, Input"]}],
                        [{"td": "Enemy"}, {"td": "   "}, {"td": ["Position, Speed, BBox, Sprite, Health, AI"]}],
                        [{"td": "Bullet"}, {"td": "   "}, {"td": ["Position, Speed, BBox, Sprite, Angle, Damage, Lifespan"]}],
                        [{"td": "Tile"}, {"td": "   "}, {"td": ["Position, Speed, BBox"]}]
                      ]}
                    ]
